<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Embraer delivers two jets.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Embraer delivers two jets.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian aircraft manufacturer Embraer said it has delivered the first two of 25 EMB-145 jets ordered by Continental Express, a subsidiary of Continental Airlines Inc.</p>
<p>Embraer will deliver two more of the jets by the end of December, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Earlier this year, Embraer signed a $375 million deal to supply Continental Express with 25 EMB-145 aircraft, with options for another 175 jets over the next 10 years, it said.</p>
<p>Embraer plans to deliver 33 jets to Continental Express in 1997 and 48 from 1998 onward, it said.</p>
<p>(( -- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
